# 07 — Vault page (pkmanager) + API json-field encryption fix

Date: 2026-10-12
Type: noolva-api change (1 file) + pkmanager react-admin change (2 files) + 1 DB seed

## What changed (noolva-api)
`api/app/routes/data_models.py` — auto-crud encryption for json/jsonb columns:
- **Write fix (bug 10042):** create/update used to bind a bare base64 AES
  ciphertext string into `json`/`jsonb` columns, so any encrypted JSON field
  (e.g. `password_vault.additional_secrets`) failed with
  `invalid input syntax for type json`. New `_encrypt_field_for_db()` for
  dict values encrypts **per value** and stores the whole object as a JSON
  string (`json.dumps({"key": "<ciphertext>", ...})` — keys stay plain,
  values are AES-GCM ciphertext; asyncpg requires a str for json/jsonb
  binding). Non-dict json values keep the whole-value JSON-string-scalar
  scheme; non-json fields unchanged.
- **Read fix (bug 2):** `_apply_field_masking()` used to call
  `str(val)` before decrypting, so a legacy plaintext JSON object came back
  as a Python repr (`{'account_code': 'HSDEV'}` — single quotes, not valid
  JSON). Now only strings are decrypted, failures fall back to the raw
  value, and decrypted plaintext for json fields is parsed back to an
  object for the client. New `_decrypt_json_field_map()` decrypts the
  per-value map (legacy whole-blob ciphertext, stringified maps, and
  plaintext maps all supported).
- New helpers `_is_json_field_type()`, `_encrypt_field_for_db()`,
  `_decrypt_json_field_map()`; all 4 masking call sites pass `json_fields`.

